{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Part B of #13 (same worktree, same branch `13-contract`, on top of your part A commit). Do not delegate further. Read the rulings again if needed: `gh issue view 13 --comments`.\n\nRename everything to `delegate`:\n1. Cargo package name `delegate` (Cargo.toml + Cargo.lock), version `1.0.0`. Crate imports in tests become `delegate::...`.\n2. Host profile: default path `~/.config/delegate/host-profile.json` (respect XDG_CONFIG_HOME the way the code already does), override env `DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE`. Drop `CURSOR_DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE` outright (no alias).\n3. Status records: only `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/`. Remove any remaining `cursor-delegate-jobs` path and merge duplicate path helpers into one.\n4. `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`: name `delegate`, version `1.0.0`, description rewritten for the CLI (one sentence: routes tasks to cursor-agent, pi or Claude Code models through the `delegate` CLI), keep author as is, keep `\"skills\": [\"./skills/delegate\"]`, REMOVE the `mcpServers` block. `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`: marketplace name `delegate`, plugin name `delegate`, versions `1.0.0`, descriptions updated, owner unchanged.\n5. `bin/setup.sh` rewrite (keep it small, keep DRY_RUN and the `run` helper):\n   - need cargo; warn if cursor-agent missing;\n   - build release into `${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/delegate/target`; copy the `delegate` binary to `$HOME/.local/bin/delegate` (mkdir -p); warn if `$HOME/.local/bin` is not on PATH;\n   - profile migration: old = `${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/cursor-delegate/host-profile.json`, new = `.../delegate/host-profile.json`. If new is absent and old exists: mkdir + mv old → new. If both exist: print a note, touch neither. If neither: do nothing (no scaffolding — the binary has built-in defaults);\n   - if `claude` is on PATH: `claude plugin marketplace add \"$REPO_ROOT\" --scope user` and `claude plugin install delegate@delegate --scope user`; print a one-line note that an old `cursor-delegate@cursor-delegate-local` install should be removed with `claude plugin uninstall cursor-delegate@cursor-delegate-local && claude plugin marketplace remove cursor-delegate-local`.\n   - Old names may appear ONLY in this script's migration/uninstall lines.\n   - Delete bin/cursor-delegate-mcp if it is tracked.\n6. README.md: rewrite for the CLI, short (≤80 lines): what it is, install (`./bin/setup.sh`), the six commands with one-line descriptions (exact surface from spec #4), capabilities, backends table (cursor / pi / claude, with \"pi and claude backends land in later releases\" until they exist), where status records live, host profile path + env override. No MCP. Plain English, sentence case headings, no marketing.\n7. AGENTS.md: only update if it names the old project; keep its structure.\n8. Any remaining old-name strings in src/ and tests/ (`cursor-delegate`, `cursor_delegate`, `CURSOR_DELEGATE`, `cursor_run`, `mcp`/`MCP`) are removed or reworded. Leave tests/fixtures/, scripts/, skills/, .github/ untouched.\n\nAcceptance check you must run and paste: `git grep -nI -i -e cursor-delegate -e cursor_delegate -e cursor_run -e mcp -- . ':!tests/fixtures' ':!skills' ':!scripts'` — only bin/setup.sh migration/uninstall lines may match (`--approve-mcps` in the cursor-agent argv is a real cursor flag and is allowed).\n\nChecks: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test`, and `DRY_RUN=1 ./bin/setup.sh` (paste its output) all green. Do NOT run setup for real. Commit `chore: rename to delegate and ship the CLI as 1.0.0 (#13)` ending `Co-Authored-By: Composer 2.5 <noreply@cursor.com>`. Do not push.\n\nCompletion bar: commit SHA, the grep output, DRY_RUN output, test counts — or a failure triage. Then **Friction** (≤3 bullets). End with a STATUS line.\n\nALSO (fix from part A): you deleted tests/live.rs, but spec #4 story 55 keeps opt-in live tests. Restore it rewritten for the CLI: one `#[ignore = \"needs a logged-in cursor-agent; spends a Cursor request\"]` test that runs `delegate run --model composer-2.5 --capability read-only` (prompt \"What is 17 * 23? Answer with just the number.\" on stdin) in a temp dir, then `delegate watch <id> --timeout 300`, and asserts the record is terminal DONE with \"391\" in the text and a non-empty session id. Use `env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_delegate\")`. Keep it under 40 lines. Do not run it (it spends a request); only make sure it compiles (`cargo test --test live --no-run`).\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"e2d994f1-ef61-48a1-b218-cde928b7cc82"}
